          "level": 2,
          "content": "Number Play"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.17,
            0.883,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": "**Q. Think about various situations where we use numbers. List five different situations in which numbers are used. See what your classmates have listed, share, and discuss.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.215,
            0.682,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Five different possible situations in which numbers are used -"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.242,
            0.291,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": "1. Time"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.26,
            0.32,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": "2. Calendar"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.278,
            0.441,
            0.295
          ],
          "content": "3. Counting objects/Marks"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.295,
            0.513,
            0.313
          ],
          "content": "4. Measurement of height & weight"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.313,
            0.304,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "5. Money"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.331,
            0.39,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": "There could many more."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.385,
            0.218,
            0.402
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Section 3.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.412,
            0.226,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 55**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.44,
            0.504,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": "**Q. What do you think these numbers mean?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.466,
            0.302,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Refer page 56."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.494,
            0.263,
            0.515
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 56"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.524,
            0.881,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": "**Q1. Can the children rearrange themselves so that the children standing at the ends say ‘2’?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.559,
            0.839,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "Ans. No; There will be no one standing on the other side of the child standing at the end."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.587,
            0.735,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "**Q2. Can we arrange the children in a line so that all would say only 0s?** Ans. Yes; All the children in the line should be of same height."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.631,
            0.744,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": "**Q3. Can two children standing next to each other say the same number?** Ans. Yes; Refer picture on page 55."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.676,
            0.882,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "**Q4. There are 5 children in a group, all of different heights. Can they stand such that four of them say ‘1’ and the last one says ‘0’? Why or why not?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.721,
            0.677,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Yes, they can, if they are standing in ascending order of height."
        },
